========================================================================
FSR: Finiteness Analysis
========================================================================

--- 1. UV Cutoff: p_max(l) = hbar*pi / a_l ---
  Standard QFT: p_max -> infinity (UV divergence)
  FSR: p_max(l) = hbar*pi*4^l / a  (finite at every l)
  l= 0: N_l=        44, a_l=2.90e+24 m, p_max=1.14e-58 kg.m/s, E_max=3.43e-50 J = 2.14e-31 eV
  [PASS] p_max(l) finite at l=0 
  l= 2: N_l=       704, a_l=1.81e+23 m, p_max=1.83e-57 kg.m/s, E_max=5.49e-49 J = 3.43e-30 eV
  [PASS] p_max(l) finite at l=2 
  l= 6: N_l=    180224, a_l=7.07e+20 m, p_max=4.68e-55 kg.m/s, E_max=1.40e-46 J = 8.78e-28 eV
  [PASS] p_max(l) finite at l=6 
  l=10: N_l=  46137344, a_l=2.76e+18 m, p_max=1.20e-52 kg.m/s, E_max=3.60e-44 J = 2.25e-25 eV
  [PASS] p_max(l) finite at l=10 
  l=20: N_l=48378511622144, a_l=2.63e+12 m, p_max=1.26e-46 kg.m/s, E_max=3.77e-38 J = 2.36e-19 eV
  [PASS] p_max(l) finite at l=20 
  l=40: N_l=53192736063043683687071744, a_l=2.40e+00 m, p_max=1.38e-34 kg.m/s, E_max=4.15e-26 J = 2.59e-07 eV
  [PASS] p_max(l) finite at l=40 

  Planck limit: l_max=98, N_max=4e+60
  a_min = 2.88e-35 m (Planck length = 1.62e-35 m)
  E_max = 3.44e+09 J = 2.15e+28 eV (Planck energy)
  [PASS] UV cutoff at Planck scale is finite and physical 

--- 2. 1-Loop Integral: Finite vs Divergent ---
  Standard QFT: integral diverges as Lambda -> infinity
  FSR: finite sum over N_l modes
  l= 0: N_l=      44, loop_sum = 92.129582 (finite)
  l= 2: N_l=     704, loop_sum = 1310.299797 (finite)
  l= 6: N_l=  180224, loop_sum = 3132.875292 (finite)
  l=10: N_l=46137344, loop_sum = 3141.557037 (finite)
  l= 0: FSR sum=22.720653, continuum int=1570.773600
  l= 2: FSR sum=356.663821, continuum int=1570.794906
  l= 6: FSR sum=1561.762218, continuum int=1570.796321
  [PASS] FSR sum converges to continuum at l=6 
  l=10: FSR sum=1570.443971, continuum int=1570.796327
  [PASS] FSR sum converges to continuum at l=10 

--- 3. Schwarzschild Singularity: Kretschmann Scalar ---
  Standard GR: R^2 -> infinity as r -> 0
  FSR: r_min = a_l, R^2 finite at every l
  l= 0: r_min=2.90e+24 m, K=1.77e-139 m^-4 (finite)
  [PASS] Kretschmann scalar finite at l=0 
  l=10: r_min=2.76e+18 m, K=2.35e-103 m^-4 (finite)
  [PASS] Kretschmann scalar finite at l=10 
  l=20: r_min=2.63e+12 m, K=3.13e-67 m^-4 (finite)
  [PASS] Kretschmann scalar finite at l=20 
  l=98: r_min=2.88e-35 m, K=1.82e+215 m^-4 (finite)
  [PASS] Kretschmann scalar finite at l=98 

  Planck core: r_min = L_P = 1.62e-35 m
  K at Planck core = 5.86e+216 m^-4 (finite but large)
  [PASS] Kretschmann scalar finite at Planck scale 

--- 4. Maximum Energy at Finite l ---
  Standard QFT: E can be arbitrarily large
  FSR: E_max(l) = hbar*c*pi/a_l
  l= 0: E_max = 3.43e-50 J = 2.14e-31 eV
  [PASS] E_max finite at l=0 
  l= 2: E_max = 5.49e-49 J = 3.43e-30 eV
  [PASS] E_max finite at l=2 
  l= 6: E_max = 1.40e-46 J = 8.78e-28 eV
  [PASS] E_max finite at l=6 
  l=10: E_max = 3.60e-44 J = 2.25e-25 eV
  [PASS] E_max finite at l=10 
  l=98: E_max = 3.44e+09 J = 2.15e+28 eV
  [PASS] E_max finite at l=98 

--- 5. Total Number of Modes ---
  Standard QFT: infinite number of modes (continuous spectrum)
  FSR: N_l = N * 4^l modes at level l
  At Planck scale (l=98): N_max = 4.42e+60 modes
  [PASS] Total number of modes is finite at every l 

--- 6. The l -> Infinity Limit: Divergence Re-emergence ---
  As l -> infinity: a_l -> 0, N_l -> infinity, p_max -> infinity
  All continuum divergences re-emerge in this limit.

  PHYSICAL INTERPRETATION:
  The l -> infinity limit corresponds to E -> infinity.
  Physical processes at finite energy E have finite l:
  l ~ log_4(E * a / (hbar * c * pi))

  The continuum limit is a MATHEMATICAL IDEALIZATION,
  not a physical regime. FSR is UV-complete at every
  finite energy scale.
  LHC (10 TeV) needs l = 73, N_l = 3924931154941389672910286415986111625052553216
  Planck energy needs l = 83, N_l = 4e+51

========================================================================
RESULT: 20 PASS, 0 FAIL
========================================================================
ALL FINITENESS CHECKS PASSED:
  - UV cutoff: finite at every finite l
  - Loop integrals: finite sums, no divergences
  - Schwarzschild: finite Kretschmann at r_min = a_l
  - Maximum energy: bounded at every l
  - Total modes: finite at every l

KEY CONCLUSION:
  The finite spectrum makes FSR UV-complete at every finite
  energy scale. Continuum divergences only re-emerge in the
  l -> infinity limit, which is a mathematical idealization
  corresponding to infinite energy.
